# ORCLBLNK: blink walls and both blink rays (M16.4).
#
# A blink wall is a metronome with a P3 counter, so like ORCLMECH's devices it
# accumulates and cannot sit on the title board; Blink Bay is reached over a
# board edge (see mech.scn for why that, and not a passage). Unlike ORCLMECH
# this scenario needs no `phase` directive: every stat here has cycle 1, so the
# gate `CurrentTick mod Cycle = statId mod Cycle` is satisfied on every frame
# whatever CurrentTick happens to be, and the rhythm below is exact.
#
# ElementBlinkWallTick (ELEMENTS.PAS:802) does three things in one pass:
#   P3 = 0      -> arm with P1 + 1, so P1 is a start delay
#   P3 = 1      -> if the ray is already out, RETRACT it square by square;
#                  otherwise LAY it, damaging every Destructible tile on the way
#                  and stopping at the first thing it cannot pass
#   otherwise   -> count down
# Both walls carry P2 12, so each toggles every 25 frames; the north-south wall
# has P1 0 and the east-west wall P1 12, so they run half a period apart and
# every checkpoint below shows one ray out and the other withdrawn.
#
# The north-south wall at 6,3 fires down column 6 to a solid backstop at 6,20.
# The east-west wall at 12,7 fires along row 7 to a backstop at 24,7, through a
# gem at 18,7 — a gem is Destructible, so the first ray damages it away and then
# occupies its square, and it never comes back.
#
# The player stations are the ray's player branch, which is not symmetric:
#
#   east-west ray   -> push the player one square NORTH, else one square SOUTH
#   north-south ray -> push the player one square EAST, else ... one square EAST
#
# That second "else" is a real ZZT bug, faithfully ported: ELEMENTS.PAS:845-848
# tests whether the square to the WEST is empty and then moves the player EAST
# anyway, on top of whatever was there. Both branches are exercised here. At row
# 13 the square east of the column is solid and the square west is open, so the
# player is pushed INTO the wall and stands on it with the wall saved as their
# Under; at row 10 the square east is open, so the correct branch simply steps
# them aside.
#
# A lit ray is also a wall: the player waits at 5,13 while it is out and can
# only enter the column during a retraction.
world ORCLBLNK
seed 0
boot 240
capture title
play
# Blink Hub: unpause and cross the east border opening at 60,13.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive
# Walk to 5,13. The north-south ray is lit, so 6,13 is closed.
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture at-lit-gate
# It retracts on frame 43; step into the column while it is withdrawn.
settle 16
capture gate-retracted
move right
capture in-column
# It fires again on frame 68. East of 6,13 is solid, so this is the quirk push:
# the player is moved east regardless, on top of the wall.
settle 44
capture pushed-into-wall
# Climb to row 10, where the square east of the column is open.
move up
move up
move up
settle 24
capture gate-retracted-again
move left
capture in-column-again
# Fires again on frame 118: the correct branch just steps the player aside.
settle 44
capture pushed-aside
